course: dictionary
lesson: 9102
title: Smaller
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Smaller is a comparing word. It tells you that one thing is less big than another, or that there is less of something. A mouse is smaller than a cat, because a cat is bigger.
explain: Smaller can also be about numbers and amounts. 3 is smaller than 5, because 3 has less in it. The sign 3 < 5 means 3 is smaller than 5.
explain: «All of these are normal, they fade with time, and they get smaller much faster once you tell a grown-up you trust.» Here smaller means less big. A worry feels less big when you share it. To check, swap in less big: they get less big much faster once you tell a grown-up you trust. That still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Smaller means less big, or less in number or amount.
fact: Smaller is the comparing form of small, so a mouse is smaller than a cat.
fact: The sign 3 < 5 means 3 is smaller than 5.
fact: To put numbers in order from smallest to largest, find the smallest first, then the next smallest.
fact: Smaller can describe a size, a piece, or an amount: a smaller slice of cake, or a smaller number of children.
exercise: «A mouse is smaller than a cat.» Is the mouse bigger or smaller than the cat? | *Smaller | The same as a cat | Bigger | Louder
exercise: Which number is smaller than 7? | 12 | 7 | *4 | 9
exercise: «They get smaller much faster once you tell a grown-up you trust.» What does smaller mean here? | Older | *Less big | Closer to you | Louder
test: Put these numbers in order from smallest to largest: 8, 2, 5. Which one is the smallest? | 8 | 5 | 10 | *2
test: What does 3 < 5 tell you? | 3 is bigger than 5 | 5 is smaller than 3 | 3 and 5 are equal | *3 is smaller than 5
exam: A grain of rice is ___ than a football. Which word fits best? | later | *smaller | softer | louder
